## 2. The most important game requirement

The Mystery game must be a real, top-down 2D exploration and investigation game, not a quiz interface.

The child should be able to:

- Move a character around a 2D environment.
- Explore a generated world.
- Find and investigate clues.
- Interact with objects.
- Discover evidence related to the selected learning topic.
- Solve the mystery by collecting the required clues.
- Reach and unlock an exit.
- Replay with a newly generated adventure.

AI must generate the adventure when the child starts the game, using the selected subject, topic, class and curriculum learning objectives. We do not want one fixed mystery that every child sees, and we do not want the AI to generate only multiple-choice questions.

